---
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/latin-200.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/latin-300.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/latin-300.css';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbs, website } from '../seo/jsonld';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Methodology · Scintille"
	description="What the dots on Scintille's globe are, where they come from, and what the globe cannot show."
	jsonLd={[
		website(),
		breadcrumbs([
			{ name: 'Scintille', path: '/' },
			{ name: 'Methodology', path: '/methodology/' },
		]),
	]}
>
	<main class="method">
		<a class="name" href="/">Scintille</a>
		<h1>Methodology</h1>
		<p class="lead">Lightning as satellites measure it, with its gaps.</p>

		<h2>What you see</h2>
		<p>
			One dot is one flash, seen from orbit by its light: inside a cloud, between clouds or down to the ground.
		</p>

		<h2>Sources</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>NOAA GOES-East and GOES-West lightning mappers: the Americas and nearby oceans.</li>
			<li>EUMETSAT MTG Lightning Imager: Europe, Africa and the Atlantic, being connected.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Where two satellites overlap, each flash is drawn once.</p>

		<h2>Coverage</h2>
		<p>
			Asia, Oceania and the poles are not covered, and detection weakens towards the edge of each view. An empty
			region is not a region without lightning.
		</p>

		<h2>Brightness</h2>
		<p>Follows the light energy measured for each flash, on a relative scale that is still provisional.</p>

		<h2>Delay</h2>
		<p>Flashes aim to appear within two minutes. The live delay is on the <a href="/status/">status page</a>.</p>

		<h2>Limits</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Satellites miss some flashes.</li>
			<li>A few faulty detector pixels can show a dot that keeps flashing in place.</li>
			<li>Clouds are hourly and lag the lightning.</li>
			<li>The ground is a composite image: 2004 by day, about 500 m sharp; 2016 city lights by night, about 750 m sharp.</li>
			<li>Thunder timing is stylized: it only says near or far.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Credits</h2>
		<p class="credits">
			GLM data courtesy of NOAA.<br />
			Contains modified EUMETSAT Meteosat data 2026.<br />
			Clouds: NOAA GOES-East and GOES-West, JMA Himawari-9 via NOAA, contains modified EUMETSAT Meteosat data 2026; gaps from NOAA NESDIS GMGSI.<br />
			Earth imagery: NASA Earth Observatory.
		</p>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.method {
		--ink: rgb(238 242 247 / 0.9);
		--soft: rgb(238 242 247 / 0.62);
		--dim: rgb(238 242 247 / 0.4);
		--hair: rgb(238 242 247 / 0.14);
		--mono: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
		--sans: 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif;
		max-width: 32rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: clamp(24px, 6vw, 72px) 16px 96px;
		color: var(--soft);
		font: 300 15px/1.75 var(--sans);
		-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
	}
	.name {
		color: var(--ink);
		font: 200 18px/1 var(--sans);
		letter-spacing: 0.5em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	h1 {
		margin: 56px 0 0;
		color: var(--dim);
		font: 300 10px/1 var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.24em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	.lead {
		margin: 16px 0 0;
		color: var(--ink);
		font: 200 22px/1.5 var(--sans);
	}
	h2 {
		margin: 48px 0 10px;
		color: var(--dim);
		font: 300 10px/1 var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.24em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	p,
	ul {
		margin: 0 0 10px;
	}
	ul {
		padding-left: 14px;
	}
	a {
		color: var(--ink);
		text-decoration-color: var(--hair);
		text-underline-offset: 4px;
	}
	.credits {
		color: var(--dim);
		font: 300 11px/1.8 var(--mono);
	}
	:focus-visible {
		outline: 1px solid var(--soft);
		outline-offset: 5px;
	}
</style>
